    "body": "<!-- claude-projects-attribution: {\"github_login\":\"siainbuletin\"} -->\n_Requested by **Sia** · [project thread](https://claude.ai/code/project/chan_01KaQfLZaF43QUMN3kcT7pW2?thread=cmsg_01KaQfLZaF43QUMN3kcT7pW21PoXemQ4TWuXvmmeKXUB23)_\n\n## What\n`sp-insert-note` / `sp-select-note` took seconds to open with the coloured tag column. `sp-org-tag-groups--with-tag-column` binds `vulpea-select-cache` to nil (the column width depends on the frame), so vulpea rebuilds the title and tag column of every note on each call. Per note that meant: sorting a copy of the rules, matching them, looking up the tag group with `mapcar`/`member` over the whole group alist, an `assoc`/`assq` for the colour, `frame-parameter` and `face-attribute`, and building the propertized chips again.\n\n## Change\n`sp-org-tag-groups--memoize` keeps a hash table of results for the chip face of a tag, the emoji of a tag list, and the chips of a tag list and width. The table is cleared when the rules, groups, colours, palette, tag face height, `combo-consumes`, link position or the light/dark background mode change (compared with `eq`). Notes with the same tags now cost one hash lookup. Both the `.el` and the literate doc are updated, with a CHANGELOG entry.\n\n## Not tested\nNothing was run in Emacs (none in the container); the diagnosis is from reading the code and the profile (time inside `command-execute`, not redisplay). If it is still slow, the remaining cost is vulpea's own `vulpea-db-query` of all notes, which this change does not touch.\n\n---\n_Generated by [Claude Code](https://claude.ai/code/session_01WWLNiALKhTBSGnpKY8Dseo)_",
